-- title:
--   Théorème 3 — weak cluster points of the proximal iterates (13) solve (12), and the iterates form a minimizing sequence
-- statement:
--   Let $H$ be a real Hilbert space, $C\subseteq H$ a nonempty closed convex set, and $f:H\to\mathbb R$ convex and lower semicontinuous such that every sublevel set $\{x\in C\mid f(x)\le a\}$, $a\in\mathbb R$, is bounded. Let $(x^n)_{n\ge0}$ be a sequence with $x^0\in C$ and, for every $n$,
--   $$
--   x^{n+1}\in C \ \text{ minimizes } \ f(x)+\|x-x^n\|^2 \ \text{ over } x\in C .
--   $$
--   Then:
--
--   1. every weak cluster point $\tilde x$ of $(x^n)$ is a solution of (12), i.e. $\tilde x\in C$ and $f(\tilde x)\le f(x)$ for all $x\in C$;
--   2. $(x^n)$ is a minimizing sequence: the infimum $m=\inf_{x\in C} f(x)$ is a real number and
--   $$
--   \lim_{n\to\infty} f(x^n)=m .
--   $$
--
--   This is the main result of §IV: the proximal regularization of a convex minimization problem converges in value, and its weak cluster points are minimizers. Martinet remarks that it is more precise than the corresponding result for variational inequalities (§II), where only the weak cluster points are controlled.
--
--   **Formalization Note** "Minimisante" is stated as: there is a real $m$ that is the greatest lower bound of $f(C)$ and $f(x^n)\to m$; this avoids the default value Lean's `sInf` takes on sets unbounded below, and asserts in particular that $f$ is bounded below on $C$. Weak cluster points are cluster points in the weak topology (`MapClusterPt` in `WeakSpace ℝ H`), not norm cluster points. No existence of a minimizer, and no lower bound on $f$, is assumed: both are consequences of the hypotheses. $C\neq\emptyset$ (implicit in the paper) is part of the standing hypotheses; $x^0\in C$ is part of the sequence predicate, as in "$\{x^n\}\subset C$".
-- source:
--   Martinet, Régularisation d'inéquations variationnelles par approximations successives, R.I.R.O. 4(R-3) (1970), p. 158, §4.3, Théorème 3 (announced in the Résumé, p. 154, (3)–(4))

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_MartinetReg_ConvexMin_Setting

namespace MartinetReg.ConvexMin

open Filter Topology

/-- Théorème 3, §4.3, p. 158: every weak cluster point of a sequence {xⁿ} generated by (13) is a
solution of (12), and {xⁿ} is a minimizing sequence: f(xⁿ) converges to the infimum of f over C. -/
theorem theorem3 {H : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup H] [InnerProductSpace ℝ H]
    [CompleteSpace H] (f : H → ℝ) (C : Set H) (hS : Standing f C)
    (x : ℕ → H) (hx : IsProxSeq f C x) :
    (∀ xt : H, MartinetReg.VI.IsWeakClusterPt xt x → xt ∈ solSet f C) ∧
    ∃ m : ℝ, IsGLB (f '' C) m ∧ Tendsto (fun n => f (x n)) atTop (𝓝 m) := by sorry

end MartinetReg.ConvexMin
